      "statement": "NVIDIA (2025-10-28, GTC Washington, D.C.): DRIVE AGX Hyperion 10 is 'a reference production computer and sensor set architecture that makes any vehicle L4-ready'; its production platform features the DRIVE AGX Thor system-on-a-chip (two per Hyperion 10) and 'a fully qualified multimodal sensor suite including 14 high-definition cameras; nine radars, one lidar and 12 ultrasonics'. NVIDIA 'can support Uber in scaling its global autonomous fleet to 100,000 vehicles over time, starting in 2027' on Hyperion-ready vehicles. A platform owner's target and reference design, not a purchase order: no sensor supplier is named in this release, and per-vehicle counts are a spec of this Hyperion version (time-varying, kept out of edge attributes).",
